# Product constraints

v1 is a single-page, browser-only form that builds a Slack `/remind` command and copies it.

- Keep the command keywords and time phrases in English. The reminder body may be Japanese.
- Destinations: `me`, a channel, or a user.
- Layout: one column. Destination, message, when-mode, mode-specific fields, live preview, copy.
- Choose when-mode first, then show only the fields that mode needs.
- No server, Slack API, login, templates, or generation history.
- Stay static-hostable (GitHub Pages later). Do not add a build that requires a server at runtime.
- Do not invent Slack time phrases. Offer only forms documented in `.cursor/skills/slack-remind-syntax/SKILL.md` or current Slack help.
